# User Story 1: Browse Posts and Comments - Acceptance Tests
# Test as a visitor (no authentication required)

### Test 1: List all posts (newest first)
GET http://localhost/api/posts
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK, returns posts sorted by created_at DESC
### Should return: { items: [...], total: N }

---

### Test 2: List posts with pagination (limit)
GET http://localhost/api/posts?limit=2
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK, returns max 2 posts

---

### Test 3: List posts with pagination (offset)
GET http://localhost/api/posts?limit=2&offset=1
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK, skips first post

---

### Test 3b: List posts sorted oldest first
GET http://localhost/api/posts?sort=oldest
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK, returns posts sorted by created_at ASC

---

### Test 4: Invalid limit (too high)
GET http://localhost/api/posts?limit=200
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST
### Should return: { errorCode: "BAD_REQUEST", message: "Limit must be between 1 and 100" }

---

### Test 5: Invalid limit (negative)
GET http://localhost/api/posts?limit=-1
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST

---

### Test 6: Invalid offset (negative)
GET http://localhost/api/posts?offset=-1
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST
### Should return: { errorCode: "BAD_REQUEST", message: "Offset must be >= 0" }

---

### Test 7: List comments for a post
GET http://localhost/api/posts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000101/comments
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK, returns comments for the post
### Should return: { items: [...], total: N }

---

### Test 8: List comments with pagination
GET http://localhost/api/posts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000101/comments?limit=2
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK, returns max 2 comments

---

### Test 8b: List comments sorted newest first
GET http://localhost/api/posts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000101/comments?sort=newest
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK, returns comments sorted by created_at DESC

---

### Test 9: Comments for non-existent post
GET http://localhost/api/posts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-999999999999/comments
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 404 NOT_FOUND
### Should return: { errorCode: "NOT_FOUND", message: "Post not found" }

---

### Test 10: Comments with invalid post ID format
GET http://localhost/api/posts/invalid-uuid/comments
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST
### Should return: { errorCode: "BAD_REQUEST", message: "Invalid post ID format" }

---

### Test 10b: Invalid sort value
GET http://localhost/api/posts?sort=wat
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST

---

### Test 11: Verify soft-deleted posts are excluded
# First, soft delete a post in database:
# UPDATE posts SET deleted_at = NOW() WHERE post_id = '<some-post-id>';
# Then verify it's not in the list:

GET http://localhost/api/posts
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 200 OK, deleted post should NOT appear in results

---

### Test 12: Verify comments on soft-deleted post return 404
# Using the same soft-deleted post:

GET http://localhost/api/posts/<soft-deleted-post-id>/comments
Accept: application/json

### Expected: 404 NOT_FOUND
### Should return: { errorCode: "NOT_FOUND", message: "Post not found" }

---

## Notes
- All endpoints are PUBLIC (no authentication required)
- Posts are sorted newest first by default (created_at DESC); `sort=oldest` switches to ASC
- Comments are sorted oldest first by default (created_at ASC); `sort=newest` switches to DESC
- Default pagination: limit=20, offset=0
- Maximum limit: 100
